carlhnelson@gmail.com wrote:
> Hello,  I'm about to start my (first) ascension run and I'm having some
> trouble deciding what to bring.  I am playing a lvl 30 Lawful Human
> Archeologist with maxed out stats, full set of intrinsics, and a full
> ascension kit, I think.  I have 700+ hp, AC -52, and 300 pw.

In other words, you're pretty much only worried about instadeaths and
summoning storms.  Footrice, green slime, Pestilence/Famine, Rodney or
L if your magic resistance gets stolen, etc.  None of them are
particularly deadly as long as you stay alert and watch the status line
(and keep the right resources handy).

> Even with my blessed bag of holding and STR 18/** I am still burdened
> even without my assortment of potions (20+ full healing), library of
> scrolls, bundle of wands (20+ each of fire, cold, lightning, digging,
> teleportation and cancellation) gem stash and collection of trophy
> weapons.  Do people really tend to stay unburdened on their ascension
> run?

Yes.  First, that's way too many wands.  Second, ditch the
gems/gold/trophy weapons, they only weigh  you down and give you a
higher (ie worse) score if you get them up there.

> So here are the basics of what I am bringing.  If anyone has any
> suggestions, I'd sure appreciate the help.  Oh yeah, and I have a
> saddled grey dragon.
> ----Weapons-
> +5 Silver Saber
> +7 Grayswandir

Good.  You could enchant the saber once more but that's plenty of
cuisinart power.

> 55 +7 Shuriken (I received a whole lot of advice under a different
> thread but opted to go with shuriken over poisoned darts since they
> sort of landed in my lap, so to speak)

Style points!

> Speed boots

I'd go w/ jumping instead of speed boots, especially for Astral

> small shield for when I stop twoweaponing

Ditch it, you won't want to stop twoweaponing and your AC is ridiculous
enough without it.

> -----Amulets/Rings
> several amulets of life saving,

AKA typo insurance.

> rings of FA, Lev, Slow Digestion, and Conflict

You could ditch slow digestion

> -----Wands
> 3 wands of death (0:8) (0:4) (0:6)
> 1 wand of wishing (0:1)

Excellent, having a /wishing for emergencies is a nice luxury.  There
aren't too many situations a wished-up cockatrice corpse can't get you
out of.

> 2 wand of polymorph (1:5) (0:0)

Ditch the latter (I'd ditch both, but I can see why you might want
one).

> 10 wands of digging

I'm paranoic and always carry 8, but I've never needed more than 4-5.

> 10 wands of teleport,

Keep these, they're very useful for zapping at nasties.

> 5 wands of fire,

2 is plenty.  I rarely even use one, but Elberth is possible on Astral
and they're anti-slime protection.

> 5 wands of cold

I'd ditch all but one, and you probably don't need one even.

> 3 wand of cancellation

Carry just one, the bag being double-cursed isn't likely and it's not
going to happen more than however many charges you have in the
most-charged one.

> 1 wand of probing

I'd ditch.

> -----Food
> 15 K-rations
> 6 lizard corpses

A little much (esp. on the corpses) but not _that_ much over.  I
usually carry 10 rats and 3 corpses.

> -----Scrolls
> 26 scrolls of teleport (I'll leave 1 on each downstair for the climb up
> with intrinsic Teleport Control and hope that the teleport works.)

Carry them, they'll fail often (1/3 of the time) when you have the
amulet and the mischievous force will mean you have to cross some
levels many times.

You want a few cursed ones (one to go from bottom level of rodney's
tower to top, one to go from there to vibrating square level, and at
least a couple to levelport down to the sanctum after doing the
invocation--if you levelport down to the right side, go upstairs and
try again).

> 6 blessed scrolls of charging
Nice.

> 6 cursed scrolls of gold detection

Uncurse at least 2 of them (fire and water), doing fire with confused
uncursed is much better than cursed (trust me, my first ascension was
cursed.  Ugh.)  I only use cursed for earth and the 2nd and subsequent
"home-in" tries on water, personally.

> 10 cursed scrolls of create monster (to instigate a riot on astral)

Ditch them, the last thing you want is a mob scene slowing you down.

> -----potions
> 6 cursed potions of gain level (for climbing the stairs)

Excellent, one for the sanctum and several for
asmodeus/baalzebub/juiblex stuff.

> 10 potions of full healing

Keep them, much more useful as "quaff whenever HP is at half" than to
get another measly 8 max hp now.

> 10 potions of holy water

I like a few more, 15 or so.

> 6 potions of booze

Ditch unless you don't have an expired spell.

> ---tools

You really want a lamp.  (note that if it runs out on the run, a
?charging can be used to recharge it).  You really want a light source
everywhere, actually.  Can't jump w/o it.

Good luck!



